Alembic migrations for ecomm-backend
=====================================

Config: `pyproject.toml` (`[tool.alembic]`) + `alembic.ini` (logging only).
Async SQLAlchemy engine (`mysql+asyncmy`) — handled by `env.py`, nothing to
think about day to day. DB URL comes from `ecomm.core.config.settings`, same
as the app.

Commands (all via `make`, from repo root)
------------------------------------------

| Command                    | What it does                                   |
|----------------------------|-------------------------------------------------|
| `make migrate`             | Apply all pending migrations                    |
| `make migration name="…"`  | Autogenerate a revision from model changes       |
| `make migrate-down`        | Revert the last migration                        |
| `make migrate-history`     | Show revision chain                              |
| `make migrate-check`       | Fail if models and migrations have drifted       |
| `make docker-migrate`      | Same as `make migrate`, inside the `app` container |

Raw `alembic` commands (equivalent, for when `make` doesn't cover it)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

| Command                                              | What it does                              |
|-------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------|
| `uv run alembic upgrade head`                          | Apply all pending migrations              |
| `uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "…"`        | Autogenerate a revision from model changes |
| `uv run alembic revision -m "…"`                       | Blank revision (hand-write upgrade/downgrade) |
| `uv run alembic downgrade -1`                          | Revert the last migration                 |
| `uv run alembic downgrade <revision>`                  | Revert down to a specific revision        |
| `uv run alembic upgrade <revision>`                    | Upgrade to a specific revision            |
| `uv run alembic history --verbose`                     | Show revision chain                       |
| `uv run alembic current`                                | Show the revision currently applied       |
| `uv run alembic check`                                  | Fail if models and migrations have drifted |
| `uv run alembic upgrade head --sql`                     | Print the SQL instead of running it       |

Workflow
--------

**Fresh DB:**
```bash
docker compose up -d db
make migrate
```

**Changed/added a model:**
1. Edit the model.
2. New feature package? Add its `models.py` import to `migrations/env.py`
   (next to `from ecomm.products.models import Product`) — Alembic only sees
   tables whose module has been imported.
3. `make migration name="add sku to products"`
4. Read the generated file in `migrations/versions/` before committing —
   autogenerate doesn't reliably catch renames or data backfills.
5. `make migrate` to apply, `make migrate-check` to confirm no drift.
6. Commit the model change and its migration together.

Notes
-----

- Migrations never run automatically on container start — always an explicit
  step (`make migrate` / `make docker-migrate`), to avoid multiple containers
  racing to apply them.
- Running locally against the compose `db` service (not `make docker-migrate`):
  `DB_HOST=127.0.0.1 make migrate` — don't change `.env`'s `DB_HOST`
  permanently, the `app` container needs it set to `db`.
